%% alt: Apps and agents send every model call through an AI gateway, which authenticates the caller, applies token quotas and budgets, runs policy hooks for guardrails and logging, routes to a model with load balancing, and handles retries, fallback and circuit breaking across two providers and a self-hosted model. The gateway records tokens, cost and latency per team.
flowchart TB
  A1[App A]:::human & A2[App B]:::human & A3[Agent]:::model --> AU
  subgraph G[AI gateway]
    AU[Authenticate caller]:::control --> Q[Token quotas and budgets]:::control --> P[Policy hooks<br/>guardrails, logging]:::control --> R[Router<br/>model choice, load balancing]:::control --> F[Retry, fallback,<br/>circuit breaker]:::control
  end
  F --> M1[Provider 1]:::model & M2[Provider 2]:::model & M3[Self-hosted model]:::model
  R -.->|tokens, cost, latency| O[(Telemetry per team)]:::data
